# /agents dialog (generic commandDialog over
# internal/commands/manage_commands.go's agentsModal): navigate, then its
# two action keys — "s" shows the agent's prompt, "w" shows where it's
# defined. Uses the existing commands-fixture, which defines exactly one
# subagent ("reader"), so up/down only prove the cursor-clamp guards don't
# crash with a single row — see the handback report.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/dialogs-agents.yaml
@fixture testdata/behaviour/qa/commands-fixture

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE first task
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Sure, first task handled/ 20
SHOT turn-one
TYPE second task
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Second task handled too/ 20
SHOT turn-two
TYPE /agents
WAIT 1
SHOT agents-autocomplete
# design: Terminal.dc.html:220 (CMDS entry "/agents" desc:'Manage
# subagents') — kiln's actual popup description is "View the subagents
# available for dispatch" (manage_commands.go's ManageCommands screens
# table), a real discrepancy from the design copy; asserting the design
# text here is expected to fail against the real binary.
EXPECT /Manage subagents/
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Subagents/ 20
SHOT agents-dialog-open
EXPECT /Subagents/
EXPECT /dispatched with the task tool[\s\S]*reader[\s\S]*inherit · 1 tools/
KEY down
SHOT agents-navigated
KEY s
WAITFOR /You are a test subagent restricted to reading files/ 20
SHOT agents-show-prompt
EXPECT /You are a test subagent restricted to reading files/
KEY w
WAITFOR /reader\.md/ 20
SHOT agents-where-defined
EXPECT /reader\.md/
KEY esc
SHOT agents-closed
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
